  "unresolved_questions": [
    "PWR-003 (>=600 mA on +3V3) and PWR-004 (<=500 mA from VBUS) conflict: the regulator block is sized for 600 mA capability but VBUS draw must be capped at 500 mA, so ESP32 Wi-Fi peaks must be covered by bulk capacitance rather than steady-state current. Confirm which requirement governs, or accept the bulk-capacitance mitigation.",
    "ESP32-WROOM-32 has no native USB peripheral; the pin table lists U1.6/U1.7 as USB_D+/USB_D-. Should B12 remain a direct pair to the module, or should a USB-UART bridge block be inserted between J1 and U1 (adds a BOM item and a UART interface instead of a differential pair)?",
    "Regulator choice: LDO (simple, ~0.85 W dissipation at 500 mA from 5 V, conflicts with TEMP-003 self-heating isolation) versus buck converter (cooler, higher cost and more passives against COST-002). Preference needed.",
    "ADD0 strap: tie directly to GND (address 0x48) or via a resistor/jumper to allow field-selectable 0x48-0x4B?",
    "Is a VBUS ESD/overcurrent protection block (TVS + polyfuse) desired, given COST-002 budget and that it is not stated in any requirement?",
    "MECH-003 antenna keep-out plus the TEMP-003 10 mm separation between U2, the regulator and the module must both fit within the reduced <=100 x 60 mm outline; confirm no additional mechanical constraints (enclosure, connector orientation) restrict placement further."
  ]
